Umm, that's probably your problem. When running an
XL:1 protection racket, I rarely _arrive_ at the
Mines Town temple any worse than AC:0, so if I land
the usual at least ten points of protection, I'm at
AC:-10, not AC:-4. Why on earth is your AC _still_
that bad when you've reached XL:6?

You absolutely _have to_ dawdle through the mines,
not rush, so you can lay out all death-dropped armor
in neat arrays, so your pet can confirm some of the
armor to be uncursed, so you can try it on looking
for the enchanted stuff.

Based on your other descriptions, as of heading for
the temple using a wand of digging, it looks like
you're treating the protection racket as a race.

Treat it as a leisurely stroll, instead, it works
lots better.

If you're dying in 80% of your protection runs,
you aren't getting adequate use from your pets,
and you're relying too much on Elbereth and too
little on learning how to dodge well. Most of
my protection runs, I don't use Elbereth at all,
a better use of a turn than risking writing it
illegibly.

Arriving in Mines Town with half a dozen pets
tends to take care of the "popcorn monsters with
wands" problem. The pets race on ahead and are
chewing on those monsters by the time I first see
them, so the wands never come into play except as
something else for me to ID.

When I do Sokoban on my way to the Mines Town
temple, still at XL:1 (which route is a coin flip
choice, not something planned in advance), I have
reflection half the time when I arrive at Mines
Town, which (also) helps a lot with nasty wands.

